     void fill_op(uint32_t e, ggml_tensor * dst);
 
+    // SiegeLadder P8 for prompts (on by default, LLAMA_ENGRAM_LATE_PP=0 - off): a prompt's ubatch (over 64 tokens) takes the late path as well,
+    // and set_input hands its rows to a helper thread - hashed on the main thread (the history holds the batch by then),
+    // faulted in by the helper layer by layer in the order the graph reads them; each layer's fill op waits for its own
